 description='A historian of the Canadian Prairie West who links land, public policy, racial imagery and gender. In Lost Harvests she argues that many reserve residents sought agricultural livelihoods and that policies obstructed them, challenging an inherited explanation of cultural aversion. Capturing Women examines how constrained captivity narratives and racialized images helped police colonial boundaries. The Importance of Being Monogamous makes marriage a contested part of nation-building; Imperial Plots considers women’s unequal access to land alongside their participation in dispossession. Her selected bibliography also includes collective treaty research and co-editing, with those collaborative credits retained.',
